00:03:39,581 --> 00:03:47,801
For aeons, light and dark have fought ceaselessly for dominion over the world.

3
00:03:47,801 --> 00:03:51,521
Whispers echo of a dark lord

4
00:03:51,521 --> 00:03:56,631
whose insidious grip on the realm is marked by insatiable lust,

5
00:03:56,631 --> 00:04:02,401
twisted jealousy, ravenous greed, unrelenting vanity,

6
00:04:02,401 --> 00:04:05,901
and possessive manipulation.

7
00:04:06,181 --> 00:04:16,081
A group of adventurers rose to face his threat with hidden wishes of secrets and shadows untold.

8
00:04:16,511 --> 00:04:28,171
First, there was Namu, quick as an owl in the night, a thrill-seeking thief she was, who hunted in the fringes of society.

9
00:04:28,871 --> 00:04:41,131
Next was Kora, a passionate chronomancer and hostess, whose connections to this world felt as thin as the threads of time she manipulated to build her harem.

10
00:04:42,501 --> 00:04:54,001
Faelin was a guardian of nature whose sweet, charming exterior belied her true nature.

11
00:04:54,451 --> 00:05:00,008
Descended from the heavens, Irisa brought...

12
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:07,733
Tidings of doom! Her innocent and clumsy demeanor stood in contrast to her

13
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:10,603
perfectionist tendencies.

14
00:05:12,733 --> 00:05:14,403
Lastly, Hexa,

15
00:05:14,663 --> 00:05:27,253
a bard who had yet to find her spotlight, dazzling were her performances, whilst her dreams of recognition awed where her heart.

16
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:47,003
On a warm summer night, amidst the flickering candlelight of the Singing Shark Inn, they found their fates intertwined with that of a malevolent Dark Lord, whose shadow slowly consumed everything in their path.

17
00:05:59,878 --> 00:06:03,968
Hey Faelyn, how dost thou cope with death? The fear thereof, I mean.

18
00:06:04,258 --> 00:06:13,688
Tending to my plants does help stave off the looming specter of the void, if but for a spell.

19
00:06:13,888 --> 00:06:17,388
Plants, huh? Try them once. Kill them all.

20
00:06:17,658 --> 00:06:21,058
Yes, I'm destined to bring death one way or another.

21
00:06:21,198 --> 00:06:28,988
Mayhaps thou art stuck to nursing pines rather than plants, Hexa. Nature's children are precious. Thy liver is not.

22
00:06:31,148 --> 00:06:33,748
I'll drink to that!

23
00:06:36,558 --> 00:06:43,088
Comely maiden, might I follow thee home? 'Twas my mother's wish that I follow my dreams.

24
00:06:44,208 --> 00:06:46,048
A fine distraction, Kora.

25
00:06:46,858 --> 00:06:50,838
Namu is so clever, isn't she?

26
00:06:51,108 --> 00:06:54,918
Thou mistakest me for thine accomplice, Namu.

27
00:06:55,128 --> 00:07:02,198
Canst thou not see I am trying to work my magic here? Already resorting to time magic to ensnare thy quarry.

28
00:07:02,618 --> 00:07:10,598
'Twas but a turn of phrase! I hardly need magic to court a maiden fair, merely my unending charm.

29
00:07:10,748 --> 00:07:15,548
Hast thou not enough trinkets already? I take no more than I need to survive. I promise.

30
00:07:16,598 --> 00:07:22,998
Woohoo! 'Twould seem at least someone is getting lucky tonight. Let me see. What'd you get?

31
00:07:28,918 --> 00:07:30,568
Fie! Here comes the guard!

32
00:07:30,938 --> 00:07:32,498
That is my cue to vanish.

33
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:37,498
Namu, methinks the guard doth not arrive bathed in heavenly light.

34
00:07:39,468 --> 00:07:46,178
Greetings, esteemed patrons. I seek stout-hearted souls to accompany me on a dangerous...

35
00:07:50,088 --> 00:07:51,688
How charming.

36
00:07:52,928 --> 00:07:57,668
'Tis not a journey to be taken lightly. The darkness grows stronger by the day.

37
00:07:59,958 --> 00:08:04,228
Join me, and thy deepest wish will be granted.

38
00:08:04,538 --> 00:08:06,518
Deepest wish? Sounds like a ruse to me.

39
00:08:06,668 --> 00:08:09,118
What think you? Might be.

40
00:08:09,388 --> 00:08:13,438
But what if it's not? Oi, shining lady!

41
00:08:14,618 --> 00:08:19,468
Where're you? So go on, spin us your tale.

42
00:08:19,898 --> 00:08:23,238
How can we trust thee? Who art thou anyway?

43
00:08:24,318 --> 00:08:29,468
I understand your skepticism. In times like these, we all have our doubts.

44
00:08:30,138 --> 00:08:36,578
My name is Areza. I descended from the celestial realm on a holy quest to end the dark lord's reign.

45
00:08:37,338 --> 00:08:43,088
'Tis foretold that by vanquishing the dark lord, one's heart's desires will be granted.

46
00:08:43,908 --> 00:08:46,728
What dost thou mean by our heart's desire?

47
00:08:47,388 --> 00:08:55,338
Each of you carries within you a longing that drives you. This quest can make those aspirations a reality.

48
00:08:55,518 --> 00:08:57,438
Hast thou any proof?

49
00:09:05,008 --> 00:09:08,508
There. Now dost thou believe me?

50
00:09:09,128 --> 00:09:13,918
Cora, what is wrong? Thou lookest like thou hast seen a ghost.

51
00:09:14,078 --> 00:09:18,428
What witchcraft hast thou wrought upon her, Faelyn enchantress?

52
00:09:18,668 --> 00:09:19,728
I only showed her the truth.

53
00:09:22,068 --> 00:09:25,868
Is this... the future?

54
00:09:26,368 --> 00:09:31,548
Oh, one moment. I shall return forthwith.

55
00:09:31,918 --> 00:09:35,348
Indeed, it... Where'd she go?

56
00:09:35,958 --> 00:09:39,118
Ah, she shan't be gone long. Watch, she'll return anon.

57
00:09:42,128 --> 00:09:48,428
Though it may beggar belief, Areza speaks the truth. Our wishes can be granted.

58
00:09:49,078 --> 00:09:51,698
Truly? We can wish for anything?

59
00:09:51,848 --> 00:09:53,698
Any wish.

60
00:09:54,408 --> 00:09:58,308
Well then, wherefore do we tarry? Let us away!

61
00:10:09,966 --> 00:10:13,526
諦めない強さなら
If you have the strength never to give up,

62
00:10:15,546 --> 00:10:19,106
明日が見えないのなら
and if tomorrow cannot be seen,

63
00:10:31,926 --> 00:10:37,506
僕らは 迷ってた 真っ暗 狭い部屋
We were lost in a pitch-black, narrow room,

64
00:10:37,906 --> 00:10:43,386
僕らは あがいてた 光 差すほう
struggling toward the light.

65
00:10:43,806 --> 00:10:49,286
不安や しがらみは 大きく膨らんで
Anxiety and entanglements swelled up large,

66
00:10:49,546 --> 00:10:55,006
襲いかかる 逃げ場はない 差し伸べる手も
attacking with nowhere to run, even hands reaching out...

67
00:10:55,266 --> 00:11:00,826
嫌というほどに 繰り返して
repeating so much it was sickening.

68
00:11:01,046 --> 00:11:06,646
それでも まだまだ 与えるのか
Even so, will you still give more?

69
00:11:06,646 --> 00:11:08,826
試練の日々よ
Oh, days of trials...

70
00:11:09,626 --> 00:11:15,166
諦めない強さなら それなりに平等だけど
If you have the strength never to give up, it's somewhat fair, but

71
00:11:16,046 --> 00:11:21,586
振り絞ったよ 今にもダメになりそう
I squeezed out all I had; it feels like I'm about to break.

72
00:11:21,886 --> 00:11:31,066
そんなとき ふと見上げた 先駆者たちの言葉には 同じ香り 感じたんだ
At that moment, glancing up, in the words of our predecessors, I felt the same scent.

73
00:11:42,026 --> 00:11:47,686
僕らは 夢を見た さまざま 思い思い
We saw dreams, each in our own various ways,

74
00:11:47,946 --> 00:11:53,386
僕らは 賭けてみた お互いに 全て
and we bet everything on each other.

75
00:11:53,706 --> 00:11:59,306
勝率や現実 ときには振り払って
Sometimes brushing aside win rates and reality,

76
00:11:59,526 --> 00:12:04,766
泣けばいい 悔やめばいい 途中経過さ
it's fine to cry, it's fine to regret—it's just a way station.

77
00:12:05,166 --> 00:12:10,786
夢中で 息荒く 走り続け
Lost in dreams, breathing heavily, we kept running,

78
00:12:11,046 --> 00:12:19,026
気付けば 無数の仲間たちに 支えられながら
and before we knew it, supported by countless companions.

79
00:12:20,006 --> 00:12:25,506
明日が見えないのなら その方角は間違いさ
If tomorrow cannot be seen, that direction is mistaken.

80
00:12:25,886 --> 00:12:30,566
一呼吸おいて ゼロからの近道もある
Take a breath; there's also a shortcut from zero.

81
00:12:30,966 --> 00:12:36,586
簡単じゃないことでも 複雑に絡まる前に
Even for things that aren't simple, before they tangle up complexly,

82
00:12:37,046 --> 00:12:44,726
どうか 一度 見せにおいで
please, show it to me one more time.

83
00:12:52,006 --> 00:12:55,786
出会ったんだ
We met,

84
00:12:57,666 --> 00:13:01,386
魅かれたんだ
and were drawn to each other.

85
00:13:03,946 --> 00:13:09,626
それが奇跡 君にありがとう
That is a miracle—thank you to you.

86
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:25,146
きっと 諦めない強さなら それなりに平等だけど
Surely, if you have the strength never to give up, it's somewhat fair, but

87
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:30,346
振り絞ったよ 今にもダメになりそう
I squeezed out all I had; it feels like I'm about to break.

88
00:13:30,646 --> 00:13:39,406
そんなとき ふと見上げた 先駆者たちの言葉には 頼らない 歌うよ
At that moment, glancing up, in the words of our predecessors, I will sing without relying on them.

89
